2. PLAYBOOK CONTENT — NOT covered by the MIT License
----------------------------------------------------

Applies to `src/content/playbooks/` and `public/templates/`.

Playbook content is CURATED, not uniformly owned by this project. It is not
released under a single open source license, and the MIT License above does
NOT grant you rights to it.

Each playbook falls into one of three categories:

  a) Third-party sourced. The playbook carries a `sourceUrl` field in its
     frontmatter identifying where the workflow originated. Copyright remains
     with the original author. Where the source carries its own license
     (for example an MIT- or Apache-licensed GitHub repository), that license
     governs, and you must comply with its terms — including preserving its
     license text and attribution — independently of this file.

  b) Community submitted. Contributed through the submission form on the site.
     Contributors grant this project a non-exclusive right to publish and
     distribute their submission. They retain copyright in their own work.

  c) Originally written for this project. The descriptions, setup
     instructions, tips, limitations, and troubleshooting sections written by
     this project are Copyright (c) 2026 Claude Code Playbooks, and may be
     quoted with attribution and a link to the corresponding page.

Because provenance varies playbook by playbook, we cannot grant blanket
permission to redistribute the playbook corpus. If you want to reuse a
specific playbook, check its `sourceUrl` and honor the original author's
terms.


3. ATTRIBUTION AND REMOVAL
--------------------------

Every playbook with a known origin links to that source from its page. If you
are the author of material published here and you want attribution corrected,
the wording changed, or the page removed, email
valentin.marin83@gmail.com and we will act on it promptly. We do not require a
formal legal notice to honor a removal request.

Trademarks, including Claude and Anthropic, belong to their respective owners.
This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by Anthropic.
